$ ==========================================================================
$ experimental_CaSrO.EXP  -  experimental data in DATAPLOT format
$ To overlay on the diagrams calculated with CaSrO.TDB.
$ Used with the macro comparar_experimental.TCM
$ ==========================================================================
$
$ PROVENANCE OF EACH DATASET
$
$ Datasets 1-4  (Ca-CaO liquidus, axes X = at.% O, Y = T in K)
$   Digitized in this work from Figure 3 of Deffrennes et al., Calphad 69
$   (2020) 101764. Reading uncertainty: +-0.3 at.% and +-10 K.
$   Datasets 3 and 4 are the ones Deffrennes himself DISCARDS; they are
$   included only so that the reason can be seen.
$
$ Dataset 5  (halite gap, axes X = x(Sr), Y = T in K)
$   Jacob and Jayadevan, J. Phase Equilibria 21(4) (2000) 350-356, text
$   and Table 1: x_SrO = 0.240 and 0.712 at 1100 K. Converted to the
$   pseudobinary section of the macro, where x(Sr) = x_SrO / 2.
$
$ Dataset 6  (halite enthalpy of mixing, X = x(Sr), Y = J/mol)
$   Flidlider et al. (1966) via Figure 3 of Risold et al. 1997.
$   NOT VERIFIED against the original: these are values digitized from a
$   figure by a third party. Treat as indicative only.
$
$ WARNING
$   The Ca-CaO liquidus and dfG(SrO) values appearing in
$   datos_experimentales_parrot.md and in ca_o_liquidus_solubility.csv are
$   NOT used here: they are wrong. The liquidus gave 0.99 at.%O at 1165 K,
$   below the eutectic composition (1.70 at.%O at 1094.6 K), which is
$   thermodynamically impossible; it looks as though the discarded Zaitsev
$   points were mixed in under the Fischbach label. Those of dfG(SrO) were
$   some 26 kJ/mol too negative.
$ ==========================================================================


$ --- 1. Fischbach (85Fis), differential thermal analysis. ACCEPTED by [1]
DATASET 1 Fischbach DTA
